  "limitations": [
    "All three v0.7.0 beta.3 lanes bind engine source 2c6f423bd817b6534158553e1b34ab4959c43165 and published model version 3 81f924d4. Runtime eligibility does not grant candidate-bound external-install acceptance, G4 approval or product publication.",
    "The RTX 5090 ships the exact checked first build, server 55f0b95a, under a founder-approved reproducibility exception. Neither its original nor corrected second-build pair is bit-identical. nvcc cudafe++ random module IDs are reproduced on individual translation units; attributing all 177 remaining corrected-pair ELF differences to that cause is inference. Deterministic module IDs remain a follow-up.",
    "The new unmodified upstream OMP 18.14.0 client has no appliance commands. Host-free review is not live inference or route acceptance; no predecessor platform or documented-route receipts transfer.",
    "RTX 5090 retains profile qwen38-5090-v0.13.0, semantic configuration 751d22dc, 131072 context, 146368 automatic BF16 KV tokens, DFlash2 K7, two active lanes plus two extra device-state slots and 180-second pending timeout. Fit-dependent C2 is not constant-batch-two or a fairness guarantee.",
    "Native profiles remain INT8 MTP3 C1 with Group64 A8 compiled off, 131072 context/KV, strict origin authentication and sequential UUID-bound serving on port 18082. RTX 4090 uses 640 MiB admission headroom, two extra device-state slots and 15506063360 Host bytes; RTX 3090 uses 768 MiB, four extra slots, 12284837888 Host bytes and a 350 W serving cap. No native DFlash2, vision or smaller-host qualification.",
    "Native schema 3 stores use session-checkpoints-v3 under each immutable component instance. Keep old model/root bytes untouched and replay authoritative OMP transcripts, never import old generations. The container retains /checkpoints-v013; a kept deployment-profile name does not establish cross-binary checkpoint compatibility.",
    "Strict origin authentication requires a checkpoint root and a bearer key at least 32 bytes. Within one API-key principal, prompt_cache_key names a session capability; use unique high-entropy keys and do not share the principal among mutually untrusted clients. MACs prove origin/content, not monotonic freshness.",
    "Checkpointing is best effort. Windows NTFS ntfs-write-through is not POSIX fsync or power-loss equivalence. Finite import/export and victim-validation I/O can delay decode. Disk reclamation alone does not trigger bounded rearm; Engine/admission progress or explicit client retry is still required.",
    "The #88 lane-specific export/admission reproduction and #89 installer failed-stop cleanup/checkpoint I/O follow-ups remain open trackers. Aggregate fresh runtime qualification does not close every dedicated reproduction or fault-injection item; no predecessor council approval transfers.",
    "Fresh T1, native matched C1/retrieval and bounded A8 screens do not establish global powered quality/leak parity, historical OMP parallel/fanout latency or a universal performance gain. macOS remains preview, Linux client evidence remains WSL2-scoped. Multi-GPU inference, simultaneous supported native serving, multi-tenancy and silent cloud fallback remain unsupported."
  ],
